cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use the issue-121 negative external-validation result, evidence bundle,
  or replication protocol, please cite this repository using this metadata.
title: >-
  Research README Smoketest: Issue 121 External Validation — Negative Research
  Closeout
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Liu
    given-names: Sean
repository-code: https://github.com/kodlbegiko/research-readme-smoketest
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  A reproducible negative external validation of a frozen static detector for
  install-to-first-use paths in research-software root READMEs. On 38 eligible
  GitHub repositories from JOSS issue 121, detector productization was not
  supported: recall and accuracy were below the preregistered decision gates,
  three predicted hard findings were disproved, and locked dynamic validation
  did not show that the static findings predicted first-use blockers. The
  repository preserves prediction locks, raw attempts, adjudications,
  corrections, checksums, intervention decisions, and an independent
  replication protocol. It is not a recommended README checker and no GitHub
  Action v0.2 is planned.
keywords:
  - negative results
  - external validation
  - research software
  - reproducibility
  - README
  - documentation testing
  - independent replication
identifiers: []
